Provider Endpoint URL The key Cloudflare R2 <code>https://&lt;account id&gt;.r2.cloudflarestorage.com</code> An R2 API token with Object Read &amp; Write, limited to the bucket. Its Access Key ID and Secret Access Key go in the two fields. Backblaze B2 <code>https://s3.&lt;region&gt;.backblazeb2.com</code>, as the bucket's page shows it (for instance <code>https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com</code>) An application key with Read and Write access, limited to the bucket: keyID is the Access key ID, applicationKey the secret. MinIO The address of its S3 API, for instance <code>https://minio.example.com:9000</code> — not its web console's A user or access key with the policy below. <p>A MinIO policy that gives a key exactly what backups need, on the bucket <code>odoo-backups</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::odoo-backups"]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::odoo-backups/*"]
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre>
